<%# Upstream's "Image": the picture is the card's first child, full width, and
    the card's top padding comes off so it sits flush against the edge.

    Two things are the caller's here and are upstream's component's there. The
    Card in the registry this gem ports is
    `flex flex-col gap-6 rounded-xl border bg-card py-6 …` and nothing more — it
    carries no `has-[>img:first-child]:pt-0` and no `*:[img:first-child]:rounded-t-xl`,
    so `pt-0` and `overflow-hidden` are written out. Measured on the docs page
    on 2026-08-12, where the Card also has `--card-spacing`, `ring-1
    ring-foreground/10` and a `size` — none of which is in
    `vendor/shadcn/ui/card.tsx`. That is the other registry, and it is the
    reason this looks close rather than identical.

    The footer's top padding is not written here: `card-footer` carries
    `[.border-t]:pt-6`, so giving it a border is what asks for it.

    A block of colour rather than a photograph: the gallery ships no binary
    assets, and `aspect-video w-full` is the part of the shape that matters. %>
<%= render(Shadcn::Card::Component.new(class: "w-full max-w-sm overflow-hidden pt-0")) do |card| %>
  <div class="flex aspect-video w-full items-center justify-center bg-muted text-sm text-muted-foreground">
    Where the picture goes
  </div>
  <% card.with_header do |h| %>
    <% h.with_title { "Lakeside cabin" } %>
    <% h.with_description { "Two bedrooms, one jetty." } %>
  <% end %>
  <% card.with_footer(class: "border-t bg-muted/50") do %>
    <%= render(Shadcn::Button::Component.new(class: "w-full")) { "Book" } %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
